Title: Diagnosis
Details: 
The failing test `testNullCommentEqualsEmptyComment` creates three `ZipArchiveEntry` instances with the same name "foo". It explicitly sets the comment of `entry1` to null and the comment of `entry2` to empty string `""`. It then asserts `assertEquals(entry1, entry2)`, expecting the two entries to be considered equal.

Looking at the implementation of `ZipArchiveEntry.equals(Object obj)`, the method compares the names of the entries first, and then compares the comments. The critical section is:

```java
String myComment = getComment();
String otherComment = other.getComment();
if (myComment == null) {
    if (otherComment != null) {
        return false;
    }
} else if (!myComment.equals(otherComment)) {
    return false;
}
```

This means that if one comment is `null` and the other is an empty string `""`, the `equals` method will return `false`, i.e., the entries are not equal.

This is the root cause of the failing test and also the cause reported in the current bug. The bug report points out the problem that `ZipArchiveInputStream` produces entries with `null` comment, while `ZipFile` produces entries with empty string `""` comment, so entries coming from both sources are unequal even if they refer to the same file. This mismatch breaks `Map.get()` lookup operations.

Hence, the core issue is that `ZipArchiveEntry.equals` treats a `null` comment and an empty comment as different, leading to inequality of otherwise identical entries.

The `setComment` method simply assigns the comment value, and the `getComment` method does not appear to normalize null to empty or vice versa. Therefore, the equivalence logic in `equals` needs to be adjusted to treat `null` and empty string as equivalent comments for equality checks, to avoid such mismatches.

No recent bug reports appear directly relevant to this comment equality issue.

This diagnosis explains the failing test (which expected null comment and empty comment to be equal) and the user bug report describing inequality of entries differing only by comment being null vs empty string.

